From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: do not crash when LineageSettings cannot be read

KeyGestureController reads CLICK_PARTIAL_SCREENSHOT and
VOLUME_UP_AND_DOWN_MUTE from LineageSettings.System without handling
errors. If the LineageSettings provider is missing, for example after
org.lineageos.lineagesettings has been uninstalled for the user, the
read throws and system_server crashes in a loop, so the device does not
finish booting.

Catch the exception for each read and log a warning. If the provider is
missing from the start, both options stay off, as on a device without
these settings; if a later re-read fails, the previous value is kept.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../server/input/KeyGestureController.java    | 21 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java
index 8944ca1..2d17048 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/input/KeyGestureController.java
@@ -330,12 +330,21 @@ final class KeyGestureController {
                 Settings.Global.KEY_CHORD_POWER_VOLUME_UP,
                 mContext.getResources().getInteger(
                         com.android.internal.R.integer.config_keyChordPowerVolumeUp));
-        mClickPartialScreenshot = LineageSettings.System.getIntForUser(resolver,
-                LineageSettings.System.CLICK_PARTIAL_SCREENSHOT, 0,
-                UserHandle.USER_CURRENT) == 1;
-        mVolUpAndDownMute = LineageSettings.System.getIntForUser(resolver,
-                LineageSettings.System.VOLUME_UP_AND_DOWN_MUTE, 0,
-                UserHandle.USER_CURRENT) == 1;
+        // A missing or hidden LineageSettings provider must not crash system_server.
+        try {
+            mClickPartialScreenshot = LineageSettings.System.getIntForUser(resolver,
+                    LineageSettings.System.CLICK_PARTIAL_SCREENSHOT, 0,
+                    UserHandle.USER_CURRENT) == 1;
+        } catch (Exception e) {
+            android.util.Log.w("KeyGestureController", "Failed to read CLICK_PARTIAL_SCREENSHOT", e);
+        }
+        try {
+            mVolUpAndDownMute = LineageSettings.System.getIntForUser(resolver,
+                    LineageSettings.System.VOLUME_UP_AND_DOWN_MUTE, 0,
+                    UserHandle.USER_CURRENT) == 1;
+        } catch (Exception e) {
+            android.util.Log.w("KeyGestureController", "Failed to read VOLUME_UP_AND_DOWN_MUTE", e);
+        }
     }
 
     private void initKeyCombinationRules() {
